.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1fv4z1/TASK-260715-1fv4z1_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:1429:**Orchestrator monitoring:** A valid explicit spawn creates a tracked background runner, persists run state under `.temp/spawn-runs/`, and returns a `RUN-...` identifier immediately. The response includes coordinator-facing observation hints (text and `--json observation.*`) with a seeded resume cursor (`RUN-ID:0`) and watch/events/wait commands that preserve the active executable plus board context. `spawn events` replays durable events, `spawn watch` follows the stream, and `spawn wait` observes persisted terminal state. Watcher notifications do not inject text into the active orchestrator session unless a runtime-specific adapter exists. Codex sessions launched through `task-board codex` get terminal updates pushed into the active thread; Claude Code sessions get the same non-blocking effect by running `spawn wait RUN-...` as a harness background task that wakes the session on child completion. The background runner blocks on the real child, executes the completion hook, and only then marks the run terminal.
