.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1fv4z1/TASK-260715-1fv4z1_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:3951:.task-board/EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-c1qsc6_macos-signed-distribution/TASK-260715-30lksy_assemble-macos-release-archive/README.md:10:1. A clean protected or credential-free build produces one archive with the approved host, exactly one embedded packet-tunnel provider, required frameworks and resources, relay staging bytes, manifest, notices, and no undeclared executable. 2. Bundle IDs, versions, deployment targets, architecture slices, resource names, extension point, and host-to-extension relationships match the release contract. 3. Relay files and manifest are copied by digest from the approved staging bundle and reverified after archive assembly. 4. The archive inventory, build settings, source commit, dependency locks, generator and Xcode versions, symbols, and pre-sign hashes are recorded without secrets. 5. Missing or duplicate extensions, unexpected executables or dynamic libraries, stale relay bytes, version drift, wrong architecture, dirty generation, or missing compliance resources fail before signing.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1fv4z1/TASK-260715-1fv4z1_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:3954:.task-board/EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-c1qsc6_macos-signed-distribution/README.md:10:1. The release archive contains the approved macOS host and exactly one embedded tunnel extension, bundled relay assets and notices, and exact bundle, App Group, Keychain, packet-tunnel, deployment-target, and version metadata. 2. Every nested executable is signed inside-out with the intended Developer ID identity, compatible profiles and minimum entitlements, hardened runtime, timestamps, and a passing strict signature assessment. 3. The distributed DMG is notarized, stapled, accepted by Gatekeeper on a clean supported Apple-silicon Mac, and accompanied by verified checksums, SBOM or notice links, source and relay provenance, and version metadata. 4. Private-repository publication exposes immutable versioned assets plus the stable ReluxProxy.dmg name through authenticated GitHub access, updates the stable asset without a partial window, and proves unauthenticated access is not assumed. 5. Clean install, upgrade from the supported legacy release, approved coexistence or migration, extension approval, connect or disconnect smoke, uninstall, previous-version rollback, bad-release withdrawal, and credential revocation are reproducible. 6. Production credentials are environment-scoped, masked, rotation-tested, absent from forks and retained artifacts, and release jobs are serialized with an auditable evidence bundle.
